\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {26}{\ignorespaces Architecture \textbf  {cnn1} (dataset mnist) --- per-cell wall-clock time (minutes), mean over $c_\mathrm  {tgt}$ and Gurobi seed. The two baselines $t_\textsf  {vaghar}$ (PI=off, no boosts) and $t_\textsf  {PI}$ (PI=on, no boosts) each pool together the standalone vaghar baseline runs (\texttt  {vagharNoPerturbed\_*} / \texttt  {vagharWithPerturbed\_*}) \emph  {and} the \texttt  {stdBoost} cells with all options off ($z=\textsf  {F}, \mathrm  {SG}=\textsf  {F}, \tau =0$ and matching $\mathrm  {PI}$ value), since those cells encode an identical MIP and only differ in Gurobi seed. The remaining columns are the actual boosts. In the column labels, \textsf  {z} stands for \textsf  {nn1\_zono\_bounds}, \textsf  {SG} for \textsf  {nn1\_sibling\_gate}, \textsf  {PI} for \texttt  {-{}-use\_perturbed\_intervals}, and the $\tau $ superscript is \textsf  {nn1\_relax\_threshold}. Combinations the sweep filter excludes ((PI=off, $\tau >0$); see \texttt  {run\_relaxation\_sweep.py:2854}) appear as \textsf  {---}. The two rightmost columns $t^{\mathrm  {adv},\tau =0}_{\textsf  {N2}}$ and $t^{\mathrm  {adv},\tau =0.5}_{\textsf  {N2}}$ report the advstd N2 transfer-mode runs for the two \texttt  {zono:prev\_pgd:0.0+sg} and \texttt  {zono:prev\_pgd:0.5+sg} combinations (loaded directly from the per-cell advstd CSVs that back Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:safe}); these rows only populate on the $N_2$ block since advstd is a transfer technique. The fastest entry in each row is in \textbf  {bold}.}}{77}{table.26}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:safe_wide_cnn1}{{26}{77}{Architecture \textbf {cnn1} (dataset mnist) --- per-cell wall-clock time (minutes), mean over $c_\mathrm {tgt}$ and Gurobi seed. The two baselines $t_\textsf {vaghar}$ (PI=off, no boosts) and $t_\textsf {PI}$ (PI=on, no boosts) each pool together the standalone vaghar baseline runs (\texttt {vagharNoPerturbed\_*} / \texttt {vagharWithPerturbed\_*}) \emph {and} the \texttt {stdBoost} cells with all options off ($z=\textsf {F}, \mathrm {SG}=\textsf {F}, \tau =0$ and matching $\mathrm {PI}$ value), since those cells encode an identical MIP and only differ in Gurobi seed. The remaining columns are the actual boosts. In the column labels, \textsf {z} stands for \tech {nn1\_zono\_bounds}, \textsf {SG} for \tech {nn1\_sibling\_gate}, \textsf {PI} for \cli {use\_perturbed\_intervals}, and the $\tau $ superscript is \tech {nn1\_relax\_threshold}. Combinations the sweep filter excludes ((PI=off, $\tau >0$); see \texttt {run\_relaxation\_sweep.py:2854}) appear as \textsf {---}. The two rightmost columns $t^{\mathrm {adv},\tau =0}_{\textsf {N2}}$ and $t^{\mathrm {adv},\tau =0.5}_{\textsf {N2}}$ report the advstd N2 transfer-mode runs for the two \texttt {zono:prev\_pgd:0.0+sg} and \texttt {zono:prev\_pgd:0.5+sg} combinations (loaded directly from the per-cell advstd CSVs that back Section~\ref {sec:safe}); these rows only populate on the $N_2$ block since advstd is a transfer technique. The fastest entry in each row is in \textbf {bold}}{table.26}{}}
